> the room. a few thoughts occur to this inquisitive Valkyrie:

If there is not priest and no message, it is not a "temple".  It is
a regular room that happens to have an altar.  No priest to protect it,
no obstacle to converting it if it is cross aligned.  It can be usefull
to keep *one* cross aligned altar if there are others in the game.

> Valkyrie is tempted to kick the unaligned alter just to see what happens 
> ! She supposes that by sacrificing on it, she might convert it to a Tyr 
> alter, and would she thus get much credit ?

If it is on level 21, it is either co-aligned to your diety or
cross-aligned to another one.  Unaligned altars are deeper and they are
actually to Moloch.  Your idea on conversion is correct as long as you
have enough experience.  Don't bother trying until level 5.  Long ago
if you are alive at depth 21.

